==Banknotes==
[[File:500 sol banknote security ribbon.png|thumb|200px|The 2021 edition incorporated a security ribbon. The design also incorporates [[w:Braille|Baliscano Braille]] to aid people who are [[w:Visual impairment|visually impaired]] identify the notes.]]
The issuance of the sol banknotes began in 1821, following the adoption of the [[Monetary Act of 1821|Monetary Act]] by the [[Congress of the Confederation]]. 

Before and during the [[Baliscan Civil War]], various bodies across Balisca's provinces issued their own versions of the sol, including the [[Alessandria Central Bank]] and the [[First Confederal Bank]]. Following the Federalist victory, the right of provinces to print sol on their own authority was revoked, and since then the [[Bank of Balisca]] has been the exclusive note issuing authority. 

The bank has issued thirteen new series since their introduction in 1821. The current series, Series 54.0, entered circulation on 8 January 2024, and consists of S/1, S/2, S/5, S/10, S|20, S|50, S/100, S/200, S/500 and S/1000 notes. Series 54.0 was developed in anticipation of the 200th Anniversary of the Monetary Act, with the theme "Celebrating Us". 

The artwork depicted on the sol are selected through a yearly competition which allows artists to submit paintings they want to be displayed on the next year's mint, and are then voted on by the public through the [[Open Cabildo]]. The [[w:EURion constellation|EURion constellation]] pattern is present in each of the designs.

